Hi,

the other day I got an AlphaServer 800, which is equipped with a DE500-
BA. I installed Tru64 5.0a (as I do like it but only had it on a slow 
AXPpci33 System).

Everythings fine (except for the Fact that I had to learn that some 
AdvFS Commands and LVM Features are beyond the TE-PAKs ;-)); however, 
the DE500-BA takes "rather long" to Autonegotiate in Tru64.

When the System boots into SRM it autonegs rather fast. However, in 
Tru64 it takes about 30 secs. - plus it negotiates several times. First 
when the Systems sets its time from NTP; then it seems to lose Status - 
and when its trying to mount some NFS-FS it again negotiates (and the 
NFS mount will Background). Once it managed to negotiate this second 
time it will remain "up" and stays up solid.

I already tried other Switches and Cables, but that did not help a bit. 

Is this the expected beviour of Tru64? I found some notes re. DE500-xx 
in the Release Notes, but the -BA was not mentioned there (or I did not 
see it) :-( 

Or is this fixed with one of the Patches (I must admit that I did not 
yet install them; I browsed the Notes and it seems most "only" fix 
Security-Problems, a few were re. Sybase and CDFS.

Cheers,
_ralf_




