> 
> Ralf,
> V5.8 is the latest firmware ever shipped for the AlphaServer 800, so
> no problems there.
> The DE500-BA is not a suspect either since the results are the same
> with another ethernet card.
> Whether the tu0 errors are related, I don't know but it would be
> interesting to see what happens with
> another switch, is ot possible to borrow another one?
> There's one other possibility that may be wrong with ewa0_mode. There
> are two auto options,
> auto_negotiate and auto_sensing. You might try the latter, though with
> my own systems I found
> auto_negotiate gave better results with cheap unmanagable switches.
> Hans

Hi Hans,

thanks for the reply - and sorry for my delay in reply (as it got a bit 
warmer in the last days I didn't boot the AS800).

Re. the Switch: I actually tried three until now: A D-Link DES1016D, a 
Netgear FS108, and a D-Link DGS-1008D. All three show the same symptons 
:-(

I just tried to set ewa0_mode to auto-sensing -- however, it seems my 
AS800 SRM doesn't "know" this mode; set ewa0_mode auto-sensing and set 
ewa0_mode auto_sensing lead to errors (bad value). Also, it's not in the 
List of valid modes and just set ewa0_mode auto selects auto-
negotiation.

Well, I think I'll live with this. I use the AS800 to setup a Forte 
Development Environment (Version 3, TOOL) to resemble a Setup we ran on 
a AS1200 (with True64 4.0)  ~12 Years ago. For this purpose the System 
just works nice, despite this little drawback ;-)

Thanks again!
Cheers,
_ralf_



